ss count per ticket so the relocated walk cost is observable.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.785,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["'Each signed event missing from the sweep's map falls back to up to two unbounded git log walks'","'The between-ticket yield (_sweep_should_yield) sees only a current holder and cannot shorten one ticket's fold.'","ABSENCE: no metric/log for pre-resolution duration or miss-count; Follow-up defers the 'how often sweep misses the map' question to a read-only server check"],"finding":"The plan relocates the unbounded git-log walks outside the store lock via preresolve_unmapped_positions, but does not state whether pre-resolution is itself bounded or yields during a sweep, nor adds any instrumentation (metric/log) for how long pre-resolution takes or how many map-misses occur per ticket. On the 300k-commit clone each miss is a ~140s walk; a sweep with many misses could now stall for minutes outside the lock with no operator visibility.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f617a98e2355cc3e2","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1-2; Root cause (_sweep_should_yield)","norm_id":"n4eb7dd6919041011","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A sweep on a large clone encounters many map-misses; pre-resolution runs serially outside the lock for minutes with no yielding and no log of progress."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attri